>>
>>
>>
>> So. Idlework from the irc chat is working on a CMS based on Django. It's 
>> going to be not just a wiki but rather an intergration of jvs, wiki, 
>> CLL.....
>> Good luck to him. 
>>
>> However, don't you think that there is a problem here, namely a split of 
>> efforts?
>>
>> We can't be sure whether he finishes this project and we shouldn't wait 
>> either.
>>
>> So I suggest once again leaving the old wiki as it is.
>>
>>
>> Now let's think that Lojban has been just born. What do we need for a 
>> wiki?
>>
>> 1. Textbook (the Waves) and a link to CLL.
>> 2. Texts, multimedia with links to them.
>> 3. Some brief informaton about the history of the language.
>> 4. Some brief information about the difference between CLL and the 
>> current state of affairs (but it's better to move it into the Waves).
>>
>>
>> That's all! Have I missed something?
>>
>> This is how we can start working on the new wiki (mw.lojban.org).
>>
>> If Idelwork succeeds then we'll transfer the content of LMW and the whoe 
>> jvs database into his project.
>> Until then let's use the best we have.
>>
>> Feilen, I hope these 4 items are clear enough. Make the wiki the way you 
